course: dictionary
lesson: 7090
title: Short words: abbreviations
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word. PE is short for physical education, so when you see PE on the timetable, it means the lesson where you run, jump, play games and learn to keep fit.
explain: Context helps you spot it. «On PE day you wear or pack the sports clothes and trainers the school asks for.» Sports clothes and trainers tell you PE is a lesson about being active, so PE must mean physical education.
explain: Capital letters are a clue. PE is written with capitals because each letter stands for a word: P for physical and E for education. When you meet an unknown short form, check the full word in a dictionary.
fact: PE is an abbreviation (a short form) of physical education.
fact: «PE lesson», «PE kit», «PE teacher» and «in PE» all use PE to mean the school subject.
fact: PE kit means the sports clothes and trainers you change into for a PE lesson.
fact: «Schools often keep spare kit, like swimming costumes and PE shoes, and lend it quietly to children who need it.»
fact: Some abbreviations have full stops, like Mr., and some do not, like PE.
exercise: What does PE stand for? | Play equipment | Pupil experience | *Physical education | Personal exercise
exercise: «On PE day you wear or pack the sports clothes and trainers the school asks for.» What do children wear on PE day? | *Sports clothes and trainers | A coat and wellies | Their best party dress | Pyjamas and slippers
exercise: Which sentence uses PE as a school lesson? | We have a pe in the garden | We have peas for tea | We have a pet in class | *We have PE after lunch on Tuesdays
test: What is a PE kit? | A kit for fixing bikes | A spare pencil case | A kind of pet | *The sports clothes and trainers you change into
test: Dad's checklist has «PE kit, reading book, inhaler, charger». What is the PE kit on the list? | *Sports clothes and trainers for PE | An inhaler | A reading book | A phone charger
exam: What is the full meaning of the abbreviation PE? | Pupil excellence | Pets and environment | *Physical education | Practice English
